            <h1>About the Site</h1>
<p>This is mostly a public reflection of things I've written in my physical notebooks. I'm a fan of first thinking with <a href="pens">pen and paper</a>.</p>
<p>The visual style of the site is meant to emulate writing in a Rhodia Sapphire dot-grid notebook
with Waterman's Serenity Blue or Pilot's Iroshizuku Kon-peki ink, though I've limited myself to <a href="https://www.w3schools.com/cssref/css_colors.asp">css named colors</a>. The font is <a href="https://dtinth.github.io/comic-mono-font/">comic mono</a>.</p>
<h2>Hosting &amp; Rendering</h2>
<p>This site is hosted on <a href="https://github.com/toombs-caeman/toombs-caeman.github.io">github</a> currently. The content is not and probably never will be interactive, so pages are rendered statically.</p>
<p>Rendering is done with a <a href="https://www.nushell.sh/">nushell</a> script delegating the heavy lifting to the <a href="https://gitlab.com/jobol/mustach/">mustach</a> and <a href="https://github.com/mity/md4c">md4c</a> packages for <a href="https://mustache.github.io/">mustache templating</a> and <a href="https://github.github.com/gfm/">markdown rendering</a></p>
<p>Rendered files are saved in git so that the deployed site is totally static.</p>
<h2>Directory Structure</h2>
<p>Scripts used to render and test the site are in <code>/bin/</code>.
The original markdown in <code>/src/</code> is rendered into <code>/</code>.
Static files (which shouldn't be rendered at all) are in <code>/inc/</code></p>
<p>In general, <a href="https://sive.rs/su">short urls</a> are preferred.</p>
<p>There are a lot of half-written and/or broken pages floating around that simply aren't linked from the main page. You could find them if you cared to, simply by looking at the source files on github. I don't care to keep that truly hidden.</p>
<h2>Why</h2>
<ul>
<li><a href="http://www.paulgraham.com/words.html">pg on words</a></li>
<li><a href="https://jvns.ca/blog/2023/06/05/some-blogging-myths/">blogging myths</a></li>
<li><a href="https://bastian.rieck.me/blog/posts/2023/writing_why/">why write</a></li>
</ul>

